{
  "name": "How to Ensure Your Kitchen Layout is Truly Accessible",
  "step": [
    {
      "name": "Step 1",
      "text": "Making sure your kitchen is genuinely accessible goes beyond just lowering a counter. It's about creating a cohesive, functional space that supports your needs. A great accessible kitchen considers several key aspects in unison. Start by looking at your current reach ranges and sight lines; are things you use daily within easy reach? Next, evaluate your traffic paths – you'll want plenty of clear floor space for comfortable movement and turning, especially important for wheelchair users. Think about your storage zones, too. Are your most-used items easily accessible, perhaps in pull-out drawers or on lowered shelves? Don't forget about appropriate lighting to improve visibility and safety. Lastly, consider appliance placement; ensure controls are reachable and that there's adequate landing space. The real trick is to treat these not as separate changes, but as interconnected parts of a single workflow. If you're tackling plumbing or electrical adjustments, or need custom clearances for specific mobility needs, it’s definitely a good idea to bring in a professional. HH Remodeling LLC is based in Aurora and serves the entire Denver area, and we're experts in tailoring these modifications to your exact specifications. Give us a call at 303-505-0866 to discuss your project.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1
    }
  ],
